= Using the dynamicarray class =

The [../classes/html/classdynamicarray.html dynamicarray class] allows you to store an arbitrary number of values and access them with array-like syntax.  Since the dynamicarray class is template-based, you can store arbitrary types of values.

Internally, the class stores values in a series of extents.  The size of the initial and incremental extents are defined in the constructor.  The array grows automatically as new elements are set beyond its current capacity.

The following example creates a dynamicarray of integers, sets some values, grows the array by setting elements beyond its initial size, zeroes all elements, and clears the array.

